---
name: vnv-review
description: Build a repository-grounded VnV review profile for an explicit diff, pre-deploy check, security review profile, or major surface change. Do not use for ordinary reviews, implementation, remediation, or generic security advice.
type: agent-skill
title: VnV Review
okf_status: active
tags: [internal, security, performance, review]
---

# VnV Review

Emit the exact profile in `references/PROFILE-SCHEMA.md`; print it unless the
user supplies `--out=<path>`.

## Procedure

1. Resolve scope: default `git diff master...HEAD`; support `--scope=staged`,
   `--scope=commits=A..B`, and `--include-uncommitted`. Refuse a dirty tree
   unless uncommitted work is explicitly included.
2. Discover durable guidance: prefer `docs/vnv/AGENTS.md`; fall back to
   `Vnv/AGENTS.md`. Refuse if neither exists. Treat `Vnv/` as an evidence root
   when guidance routes SARIF, findings, coverage, or results there.
3. Read every immediate `<guidance-root>/*/AGENTS.md`. Parse `Scope`, `Tools`,
   `Review Focus`, references, and the declared findings target. Never infer a
   missing tool list from generic knowledge.
4. Map changed files in declared order; first scope match wins. Cross-cutting
   lanes match only their own paths. List unmatched paths under `(unmapped)`.
5. Lift must-run commands verbatim. Reference only headings from
   `SECURITY_TOOLS.md`, `PERFORMANCE_TOOLS.md`, and `SEO_GEO_CHECKLIST.md`;
   never inline their bodies.
6. Add one-line threat prompts for new HTTP routes, external integrations,
   persistence, or user-facing surfaces.
7. Emit scope, subsystem map, must-run commands, optional references, prompts,
   findings targets, rules, unmapped warnings, and evidence-root distinction.

## Boundaries and outcomes

- Never edit SARIF, findings, source, plans, or tool catalogs; never run repairs.
- Do not expose models, scoring formulas, credentials, proprietary prompts, or
  private evidence in the profile.
- Retry discovery at most once with materially new scope evidence.
- Return `PROFILE`, `REFUSED_DIRTY_SCOPE`, `REFUSED_NO_VNV`, or
  `REFUSED_ALL_UNMAPPED`, plus scope, evidence, warnings, and blocker.
